  "limits": [
    "B40 covers monitor death during one active iteration with the optional resource guardians disabled.",
    "The native workload closes its output descriptors before it detaches the writer. Docker calls are external substitutes in B40.",
    "The separate real-system batch revalidates B27 through B38 selected Docker cases. It does not inject monitor death into a Docker workload.",
    "Monitor death during benchmarks and admission boundaries remains open. The running-job check does not establish monitor progress.",
    "Simultaneous driver failure, late creation, inherited output pipes, storage faults, failed stops, and complete writer discovery remain open.",
    "The model uses atomic actions and weak fairness. It does not prove implementation refinement, durable publication, or a wall-clock bound.",
    "The bootstrap archive identifies 980285d4c. Separately hashed runtime files identify the tested candidate.",
    "Source snapshots bind bytes, not execution coverage. Raw digests do not imply publication or durable upload.",
    "All four claims, nine gates, D2, D3 reserve bounds, hosted enforcement, human review, and acceptance remain pending."
  ],
